<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE module PUBLIC
    "-//Checkstyle//DTD Checkstyle Configuration 1.3//EN"
    "https://checkstyle.org/dtds/configuration_1_3.dtd">

<!--
  The half of CI a parser can answer, run by the pre-commit hook in .githooks and by nothing else.

  Every rule here is one CI already fails on. The `lint` profile in the root pom hands javac Error
  Prone with `-Werror`, so a finding of any check it leaves on stops that build; the checks below
  are the ones whose question needs a parse tree and nothing more. That run needs `clean` and
  costs twenty minutes, so a finding first reaches the author long after the push. This is the
  same question asked of a parser, cheaply enough to answer before the commit is written.

  What each mirrors:

    UnusedImports          RemoveUnusedImports
    UnusedLocalVariable    UnusedVariable
    EqualsHashCode         EqualsHashCode
    FallThrough            FallThrough
    ModifierOrder          ModifierOrder
    ArrayTypeStyle         MixedArrayDimensions
    MatchXpath             NonApiType

  What a rule here refuses is never more than what the check it mirrors refuses, because a rule
  that is stricter stops a commit CI would have accepted. It may refuse less, and where it does the
  comment on the rule says what it leaves to CI.

  NonApiType is asked of the eight collection classes it names at any visibility: `ArrayList`,
  `LinkedList`, `HashSet`, `LinkedHashSet`, `TreeSet`, `HashMap`, `LinkedHashMap` and `TreeMap`.
  Error Prone visits the methods and constructors that a record does not own, and in each the type
  of every parameter and of the result, looking into type arguments, so `Map<String, ArrayList<X>>`
  is found as `ArrayList<X>` is, and so is `List<? extends ArrayList<X>>`. This rule visits the
  same and no more:

    - a method or constructor that a record owns is not asked, though one in a class nested in the
      record is;
    - a field, a local variable and the parameter of a lambda are not asked;
    - a type that is an array, and so a variable-arity parameter, is not looked into, nor is the
      lower bound of `? super`;
    - a `@SuppressWarnings("NonApiType")` or `@SuppressWarnings("all")` on the parameter, the
      method or any class around it stands.

  What it leaves to CI: the bound of a type variable, which Error Prone reads and a parser cannot,
  and what else NonApiType names, such as an `Optional` parameter or a Guava immutable collection.
  Checkstyle resolves no types, so a class of another package that is also named `HashMap` is found
  too; nothing here has one.

  Each of these is held against Error Prone itself, which the architecture tests run over the same
  sources, so that this is not a reading of its documentation or of its source.

  Nothing else Error Prone reports can be asked here. Whether two branches are the same, whether a
  name means two things, whether an override says so, whether a call prints an object rather than
  its contents — each needs the types, which is a compile.

  One of these is stricter than what it mirrors: the case-fold rule is a search through text
  rather than a reading of types, so it would also find a `toLowerCase()` on something that is not
  a string — which nothing here has.

  UnusedVariable lets a local stand when its name is `ignored` or begins with `unused`, and it
  reads a binding only where `x instanceof T name` introduces it, not where a switch case or a
  record pattern does. UnusedLocalVariable reads all of them, so the rule stands aside for the
  names and the bindings Error Prone passes, and is asked of the rest.

  processJavadoc is what keeps the import answers the same. Error Prone reads documentation, so an
  import only a {@link} mentions is used; Checkstyle does not read it unless asked, and unasked it
  would stop commits CI would have accepted. A comment it cannot parse, such as one that writes
  `Map<String, T>` outside a tag, is reported by UnusedImports as a violation, and Error Prone
  finds nothing wrong with the same comment, so that report is suppressed. The messages are asked
  for in English so that the suppression does not depend on the language of the machine.

  That none of these is stricter than CI over the code this repository holds is a test, not a
  hope: the architecture tests run every rule here over every Java file git tracks, and CI is green
  over them.
-->
<module name="Checker">
    <property name="charset" value="UTF-8"/>
    <property name="severity" value="error"/>
    <property name="localeLanguage" value="en"/>
    <property name="localeCountry" value="US"/>
    <property name="fileExtensions" value="java"/>

    <module name="SuppressionSingleFilter">
        <property name="checks" value="UnusedImports"/>
        <property name="message" value="Javadoc comment at column \d+ has parse error.*"/>
    </module>

    <module name="TreeWalker">
        <module name="UnusedImports">
            <property name="processJavadoc" value="true"/>
        </module>
        <module name="UnusedLocalVariable"/>
        <module name="SuppressionXpathSingleFilter">
            <property name="checks" value="UnusedLocalVariable"/>
            <property name="query"
                      value="//VARIABLE_DEF[./IDENT[@text='ignored' or starts-with(@text, 'unused')]]/TYPE
                             | //PATTERN_VARIABLE_DEF/IDENT[@text='ignored' or starts-with(@text, 'unused')]"/>
        </module>
        <module name="SuppressionXpathSingleFilter">
            <property name="checks" value="UnusedLocalVariable"/>
            <property name="query"
                      value="//PATTERN_VARIABLE_DEF[not(parent::LITERAL_INSTANCEOF)]/IDENT"/>
        </module>
        <module name="EqualsHashCode"/>
        <!--
          A record that spells its own hash is not asked to spell its own equality.

          What this rule mirrors is one direction: an equality written by hand beside a hash the
          class did not write is two answers that disagree. Checkstyle also asks the other way
          round, and CI does not — so unasked, this rule stops a commit CI would have accepted,
          and the thing it stops is the safer of the two shapes. A record's equality is written by
          the compiler over every component it has and every component it is given later; a hash
          written by hand beside it is one a later component costs a collision. Answering this
          rule by writing the equality out as well is answering it by making the loss of a
          component take that component out of what the value is.
        -->
        <module name="SuppressionXpathSingleFilter">
            <property name="checks" value="EqualsHashCode"/>
            <property name="query"
                      value="//RECORD_DEF//METHOD_DEF[./IDENT[@text='hashCode']]"/>
        </module>
        <module name="FallThrough"/>
        <module name="ModifierOrder"/>
        <module name="ArrayTypeStyle"/>
        <module name="RegexpSinglelineJava">
            <property name="format" value="\.to(Lower|Upper)Case\(\s*\)"/>
            <property name="ignoreComments" value="true"/>
            <property name="message"
                      value="a case fold with no locale is the platform's, and on a Turkish one
                             `INFO` lowercases to `ınfo`: pass Locale.ROOT"/>
        </module>
        <module name="MatchXpath">
            <property name="query"
                      value="(//METHOD_DEF | //CTOR_DEF)[not(parent::OBJBLOCK/parent::RECORD_DEF)]
                             /(TYPE | PARAMETERS/PARAMETER_DEF[not(ELLIPSIS)]/TYPE)
                             //IDENT[@text=('ArrayList', 'LinkedList', 'HashSet', 'LinkedHashSet', 'TreeSet', 'HashMap', 'LinkedHashMap', 'TreeMap')]
                             [not(ancestor::*[./ARRAY_DECLARATOR])]
                             [not(ancestor::TYPE_LOWER_BOUNDS)]
                             [not(ancestor::*[./MODIFIERS/ANNOTATION[./IDENT[@text='SuppressWarnings']]
                                                                     [.//STRING_LITERAL[@text=('NonApiType', 'all')]]])]"/>
            <message key="matchxpath.match"
                     value="a parameter or a result named for the class that holds it ties every
                            caller to that class: take or return the List, Set or Map it is
                            (Error Prone NonApiType)"/>
        </module>
    </module>
</module>
